{"answer":"The recommended emergency action to temporarily simplify routing policy rules when the edge route agent is causing high evaluation latency and end-to-end latency spikes is to apply an emergency compact policy set that temporarily applies a simplified routing ruleset. Specifically, this involves sending a POST request to the control-plane API endpoint:

POST /v1/admin/policies/compact {"reason":"latency_immediate"}

This action reduces policy complexity, thereby mitigating high CPU usage and latency on the route-agent which is responsible for routing policy evaluation. Additional mitigations include horizontally scaling the route-agent by increasing its replicas.

Recovery includes running a policy pruning process to remove obsolete legacy rules and re-introducing the full rule set gradually via canary deployment to verify stability.

This emergency mitigation is documented in the routing policy engine and control-plane runbook, which provides practical diagnostics, commands, and recovery steps for latency spikes related to route-agent evaluation.","document_ids":["dsid_bec90d2205534ca9a016f244e13884e5"]}
